# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in. NEVER commit real keys.
#
# The public booking form writes to a `booking_requests` table with the anon
# key (row level security lets the public INSERT only). You read the bookings
# in the Supabase dashboard (Table editor), which uses the service role and so
# bypasses RLS — the anon/public keys can never read them back.
#
# Local development: run `npx supabase start`, then `npx supabase status` and
# copy the API URL and anon key below. Apply the migrations in
# supabase/migrations/ (supabase db reset, or the CLI's migration up).
#
# Hosted Supabase: take the project URL and anon key from Project Settings -> API.

# Browser + server: project URL and public (anon) key.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
